From: Nguyen Phan <nguyen@nguyenphan.org>
Date: Mon, 10 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] dsv41: republish kept rows at each keep

The kept states are published at each noteLive, but the loop's next noteLive may never come once the
engine goes idle: a session's last keep then sat stale in the bar until the next request. Republish
on the engine thread at each keep, so the last state is visible before the engine sleeps.
---
 zig/src/core/lane_host.zig | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/zig/src/core/lane_host.zig b/zig/src/core/lane_host.zig
index d617dec..1e65d48 100644
--- a/zig/src/core/lane_host.zig
+++ b/zig/src/core/lane_host.zig
@@ -257,6 +257,10 @@ pub const LaneHost = struct {
             const pics = r.images.len > 0; // (the tier records each picture's identity and the prompt's model ids)
             // an image span keyed by its digest (Request.cacheKey)
             _ = store.keepWith(r.cacheKey(), at, s, r.chunks, .{ .group = job.join.group, .images = pics, .media = if (pics) tierMedia(r) else &.{}, .raw = if (pics) r.prompt else &.{}, .parent = job.parent, .fork = job.fork, .lineage = job.lineage });
+            // The kept states changed: republish them now, on the engine thread, so a
+            // session's last keep is visible before the engine goes idle (the loop's
+            // next noteLive may never come, and the kept colours would sit stale).
+            job.host.noteLive();
         }
 
         /// Report a restored prefix or its failed copy; an untouched prefix remains kept.
-- 
